# Patch: carry hunk start lines through DeepSeek Harness's edit/write diff metadata
#
# WHICH PATCH: this is "patch 1 of 2" — the data half. Applied alone it changes no pixels; it
# has to be paired with patches/dsh-web-frontend-diff-start.patch to reach the screen.
#
# APPLIES TO: the SHIPPED bundled files inside the Electron asar, not upstream package source.
#   1) dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-fs/lib/index.js            (dsh-tool-fs 0.2.1-rc.2)
#   2) dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-tool/lib/client.js   (dsh-client-ui-tool 0.2.1-rc.2)
# Both paths are archive-relative, i.e. relative to the root the asar header describes
# (…/resources/app.asar). Apply from a directory that mirrors that root:
#
#   git apply -p1 patches/dsh-tool-fs-hunk-lines.patch      # in the mirror of the asar root
#   git apply -p1 -R patches/dsh-tool-fs-hunk-lines.patch   # roll back
#
# Do NOT point git apply at the installation. Use tools/patch-asar.mjs, which does the same
# edits as literal anchors AND repacks the archive header/data (member offsets + sha256)
# with a timestamped backup. This file is the reviewable form of those same edits.
#
# FRAGILITY: low. These are unminified, tab-indented `lib/` files that keep their function
# names, so an upgrade is likely to keep the anchors intact (or fail loudly if not).
#
# WHY the numbers must be threaded through four places, not one:
#   computeHunkDiffs() is the only function holding hunk.oldStart / hunk.newStart, and it
#   dropped them; presentationMeta() then re-projects each hunk through a destructure; the
#   client's narrowDiffs() rebuilds each hunk a third time from three keys; and both guards
#   (isFileDiff on the host, the inline checks in narrowDiffs on the client) would reject or
#   silently strip any field they do not know about. Fixing only computeHunkDiffs leaves the
#   transcript exactly as it is today.

